From tru64-unix-managers  Mon May 31 06:58:06 1999
From: =?iso-8859-1?Q?Helleb=F8?= Knut <Knut.Hellebo () nho ! hydro ! com>
Date: Mon, 31 May 1999 06:58:06 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary: Bus renumbering after upgrade causes LSM failing
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079042216040

Regards,managers !

=2E. and thanks.
The quick (and dirty ?) solution: renumber back the bus ids manually,
i.e in /sys/conf/HOST edit the lines

controller      scsi0      at isp0      slot  0
controller      scsi1      at isp1      slot  0

to

controller      scsi1      at isp0      slot  0
controller      scsi0      at isp1      slot  0

rebuild the kernel and reboot. The initial reason why the buses were
renumbered came to me this morning when I got to work. A Digipaq
engineer replaced some hardware long ago and then he renumbered the
buses manually before I did the LSM setup (I do not remember the reason
why). The upgrade renumbered the buses back to the order it normally is
supposed to be thus putting LSM out of order.

