Further to my summary logged on the 20/5/99.  I logged a call with Compaq
support.  A lot of things were suggested.  I'll summarise:

1.  Compaq said that they had not seen this beyond Dunix v4.0d + jumbo-2.
Wrong, a colleague has this only a few weeks ago on an 8400 with v4.0d +
jumbo-3.

2.  Try adding the disk to lsm from the GUI - this seems to work for some
customers.  Well it didn't work for me, but the command used by the GUI was
slightly different that which I was using:
   #voldisksetup -i -q -n rz144

3.  The final solution is to add the disk to lsm as a simple disk rather
than a sliced disk. 
   #voldiskadd rz144c  (rather than rz144)
Now this worked ok - its fine.  I removed the disk and tried adding as
before (rz144) but this just failed again.  Now, even though the disklabel
'looked' ok, there must have been something screwy about it, as adding it
again as a simple disk failed.  It succeeded (as a simple disk) after I
zapped and recreated the disklabel.

4.  Try rebooting.
This sort of worked.  Prior to a reboot, I had 4 disks (all were stripe sets
on two separate HSZ70's on two separate host controllers) which would not
add.  After the reboot, 3 added ok but one was problematic.  This was the
disk which does add as a simple disk.  I could possibly have resolved this
by another reboot, but its a production box and time slots are hard to get.


Regards - Tony


