To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: 3com etherlink XL PCI combo card & Treu64 Unix
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079042215915

Dear friends, 
thanks for your replies. 
Unfortunately the answer is that the card is NOT supported.

Here the replies:

alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com
	Digital rarely supported random 3rd party add-on hardware
	since we had more than enough work just to support our
	own hardware.  I've seen little to suggest that Compaq
	will treat things any differently.  If you have a 3rd
	party piece of hardware you want to use, you should see
	if the vendor can provide a driver.

"Dr. Tom Blinn, 603-884-0646" <tpb@doctor.zk3.dec.com>
	Ask 3Com.  Unless 3Com have written a driver for that card and deliver it
	through their own channels of distribution, it's not supported.  There is
	no driver for that option in the standard Tru64 UNIX distribution, and in
	addition, there is no driver for it in the console firmware, so you could
	not use it, for example, to install the system over the network.

aad@nw.verio.net
	My experience with 3com cards on other platforms is that they're junk anyway.

Jason Orendorf <orendorf@alf.dec.com>
	Software Product Descriptions for Compaq products describe what
	devices and configurations are supported.  These are accessible
	from
	http://www.digital.com/SPD/
	The Tru64 UNIX SPD does not list the 3Com card as a supported
	option.

"Hoai Tran" <Tran.Hoai@a2.abc.net.au>
	I do not think so.


