From tru64-unix-managers  Fri May 14 21:34:02 1999
From: Oyanarte Portilho <portilho () fis ! unb ! br>
Date: Fri, 14 May 1999 21:34:02 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [Summary] what /usr/tcb/bin/dxchpwd does?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079042215744

Hi Gurus,

Thanks to

Bruce B. Platt
Jim Fitzmaurice
Andy Johnson
claudia burg
Terry Cozard

I consulted man in a box running DU 3.2 but it is not available.
Later I figured out I could have accessed it in the other boxes
running more recent DU versions. Anyway, Bruce was kind enough
to send me a copy of man dxchpwd. In short, it is a graphical
interface to change passwords. Presumably, it is the window that
opens when one has his/her password expired and the system offers
the chance to change it.

Therefore our hacker was using that interface to change passwords
in remote systems. Fortunately his activities were detected. Of 
course our passwords are not safe either. The case is being dealt 
with the due care.

Thanks to all,

	Oyanarte Portilho
	Institute of Physics
	University of Brasilia, Brazil

