Hello All. Bit of a problem with an upgrade from Digital Unix 4.0A to =
4.0B on a 255 233Mhz Alpha Workstation. We have two old 130 versatec =
SCSI controllers attached to this machine. The controllers convert from =
SCSI to Versatec Parallel Interface.To send plots to our Xerox printers. =
After the firmware and updateinstallation the controllers no longer =
function. During the boot process they are initialized, and the response =
is "unable to open device rmt0h: Permission Denied" (they are devices =
rmt0h and rmt1h). The controllers appear as tape drives to the firmware =
and are present and appear fine. They display as mkb100.1.0.12.0 Mkb100 =
Tk50 and mkb200.2.0.12.0 Mkb200 Tk50. They are controlled via =
pkb0.7.0.12.0 pkb0 Scsi Bus id 7. The Kernel also has them listed (this =
includes the new kernal after update). We have six of these controllers =
and require them for all our large scale print operations, we also need =
ultimately to progress to 4.0D of Digital Unix. To enable printing I =
renamed the new kernel and used the old kernel, not a good situation for =
the alpha machine, but it's a live system and we need to print. Any =
ideas appreciated.

