Subject: SUMMARY: how to get tcpwrappers to mail info
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079042215578

Many thanks to:

Mike Iglesias <iglesias@draco.acs.uci.edu>
Richard Bemrose <rb237@phy.cam.ac.uk>
Mandell Degerness <Mandell.Degerness@gems2.gov.bc.ca>
Robert R. Schneider <robert@pe.utexas.edu>

I had several problems.

1) Aparantly TCPwrappers stops processing when a match is made.
2) I was using the wrong mail program
3) I needed a subject switch

Solution:

# Hosts.allow
#
telnetd: 128.115.2., [... as many hosts as you want,] 128.115.82.:\
 spawn = /usr/sbin/safe_finger -l @%h | /usr/bin/mailx -s "%H-%h-%d" rnfrank@llnl.gov &

1) Attach the spawn line to the initial telnetd line
2) use "mailx" rather than "mail"
3) do  "mailx -s"

Thanks again for the GREAT and SPEEDY help.
                                            rich frank

