From tru64-unix-managers  Tue May 04 22:29:33 1999
From: Bell Jonathan <jonathan.bell () minedu ! govt ! nz>
Date: Tue, 04 May 1999 22:29:33 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Erratic tape backups
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079042215476

Hi 

Some time ago I wrote to the list about problems I was having with backing
up or restoring from a TZ88 tape drive to a AS800 server with messages such
as the following.

vdump: unable to write to device </dev/nrmt0h>; [5] I/O error

After changing or replacing all related parts I finally have a solution. A
Compaq service person in Australia found that there is an 'incompatibility'
between AS800 hardware and KZPAA scsi cards. We replaced the KZPAA with a
KZPDA and have had no problems since, 5 days worth of testing.

I pass on this information as several others ( Carlos Chua, Guillaume
Bourque to name but two ) also appear to be having very similar problems
although with different hardware. Hopefully this will help point to a
solution for you.


Jonathan Bell

From tru64-unix-managers  Tue May 04 22:10:30 1999
From: Kevin Erickson <kevine () ncrinc ! com>
Date: Tue, 04 May 1999 22:10:30 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY:Xserver configuration
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079042215475

Thanks go to Lance Berc and Robert Maiello.  
They both pointed out that I was placing the Xserver configuration
modifications into the wrong configuration file.  
They also gave me some additional setting to try.

The Xserver configuration file(s) are:
for CDE -	/usr/dt/config/Xservers	
		(copy it to /etc/dt/config/Xservers before modifying, RE:
dtlogin man page)
and for XDM -	/usr/var/X11/xdm/Xservers

Modifying the Xservers entry:
	:0 Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X :0 
to
	:0 Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X :0 -screen 1024x768 -vclass
PseudoColor

solved the resolution problems the application was experiencing!

--------------ORIGINAL MESSAGE --------------------
I am trying to get a demo package of a groundwater modeling product - GMS -
running on a personal workstation 500au.  When I run the product, the button
area of the product's toolbox is not in a displayable resolution.  It's as
if the screen resolution is not set high enough.  The system is loaded with
a full installation of Tru64 v4.0D, Patch Kit #3.  It has the 4D50T graphics
card, with Open3D v4.92 and the OpenGL license PAK installed.  

I've been told to try setting the system to 12 bit color.  But I am not
entirely certain how to accomplish this.  I have tried the following line at
the bottom of the file /usr/var/X11/Xserver.conf:

-vclass TrueColor -screen 1024x768

with no noticeable change.
Can someone let me know how to get this workstation to 12 bit color under
either CDE or Dxsession?  Or, if you are running this BOSS International
product, any details on customizations made would be appreciated.

